.\" Neo-PostOffice manual page. LGPL-2.1, like the program.
.TH POSTOFFICE 1 "@PO_MAN_DATE@" "Neo-PostOffice @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
postoffice \- Neo-PostOffice, an X11 mail client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B postoffice
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.RI [ "FLTK options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Neo-PostOffice
is a graphical e-mail client for X11, built with FLTK.
It is the modernized continuation of Pim van Riezen's PostOffice 0.7.3.
.PP
It reads mail from
.B POP3
and
.B IMAP4
servers (over TLS, with its own certificate store),
.B Maildir
and
.B MH
(nmh) folders and
.B mbox
files, and sends mail through an SMTP server (STARTTLS or SMTPS, with
login).
Messages are sorted into folders by filter rules; it has threading, a
search window, an address book that completes addresses while you type,
replies and forwards, Redirect, format=flowed text, printing through
.BR lpr (1),
and readable text for HTML-only messages (nothing is fetched from the
network).
.PP
On the first start a wizard asks for your name, e-mail address and,
optionally, a POP3 server.
Everything else is set in
.BR Config .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
The standard FLTK options are also understood, among them:
.TP
.BI \-display " host:display.screen"
The X display to use.
.TP
.BI \-geometry " WxH+X+Y"
Size and place of the main window (otherwise the last ones used).
.TP
.BI \-name " name"
The window class name.
.TP
.BI \-scheme " name"
The FLTK look:
.BR none ", " plastic ", " gtk+ ", " gleam " or " oxy .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.postoffice/resource.rc
All settings: identities, mailboxes, folders and filters, the address
book, window layout.
Readable only by you, since it holds passwords.
It is saved a moment after anything changes, through
.I resource.rc.tmp
and a rename, so it is never left half written.
.TP
.I ~/.postoffice/*.box/
The local copy of each mailbox (messages, index, read state).
.TP
.I ~/.postoffice/certs/
Server certificates you chose to trust, one PEM file each.
.TP
.I ~/.postoffice/tmp/
Attachments opened from messages; emptied when the program starts and
quits.
.TP
.I ~/.mh_profile
Read for MH mailboxes without a directory of their own.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Where
.I .postoffice
is kept.
.TP
.B MH
Another MH profile instead of
.IR ~/.mh_profile .
.TP
.B VERBOSE
A number; 1 or more prints what the program does on standard output.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X display, when
.B \-display
is not given.
.SH NOTES
Usenet (NNTP) news was removed in 0.8.1 and the SQL mailbox in 0.9.4;
mailboxes of those kinds are removed from the settings, with a notice,
when a newer version first starts.
.PP
The full documentation is the
.I README.md
installed with the program (in
.IR @PO_FULL_DOCDIR@/ ).
.SH BUGS
Report them at
.UR https://github.com/dleecurt/Neo-Postoffice/issues
.UE ,
or with Info \(-> Build Configuration \(-> Bug Report, which fills in the
version details.
.SH AUTHORS
PostOffice was written by Pim van Riezen.
Neo-PostOffice is maintained by dleecurt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lpr (1),
.BR mh-profile (5),
.BR fetchmail (1),
.BR getmail (1)
